  "worked_solution": "The general solution to the given differential equation is\n\n$$\nP(t)={P}_{0}\\,{e}^{0.11t},\n$$\n\nwhere ${P}_{0}$ is the initial number of rabbits.\n\nWe are given that after $8$ weeks, there were $786$ rabbits. So, substituting $t=8$ and $P(8)=786$ into our general solution and solving for ${P}_{0},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(8) & ={P}_{0}\\,{e}^{0.11\\cdot 8} \\\\ 786 & ={P}_{0}\\,{e}^{0.88} \\\\ {P}_{0} & =\\frac{786}{{e}^{0.88}} \\\\  & \u2248326.019,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places.\n\nHence, our particular solution is\n\n$$\nP(t)=326.019\\,{e}^{0.11t}.\n$$\n\nWe want to find the number of rabbits after $15$ weeks. So, substituting $t=15$ into our particular solution, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(15) & =326.019\\,{e}^{0.11\\cdot 15} \\\\  & =326.019\\,{e}^{1.65} \\\\  & \u22481\\,698,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest whole number. \n\nTherefore, there will be about $1\\,698$ rabbits after $15$ weeks.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
